      "artist": "Michael Gunther",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Temple of the Tooth, Kandy 0517",
      "description": "This painting is a good example of the distinctive Kandyan Style. Here, kneeling figures adore a series of Buddhas seated in meditation. The artist has individualized both the expressions of the Buddhas and the figures of the worshipers; each pair is individually numbered and captioned. The numbers are written using the familiar Arabic numerals (9, 10, 11, etc.), and the captions are in Sinhalese.",
      "dateCreated": "2008",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "kingdom-of-kandy-wp",
