    {
      "filename": "Vintane in India Orientalis, Ceylon.jpg",
      "title": "File:Vintane in India Orientalis, Ceylon.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Vintane_in_India_Orientalis%2C_Ceylon.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vintane_in_India_Orientalis,_Ceylon.jpg",
      "width": 966,
      "height": 1506,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Johann Theodor De Bry",
      "description": "After an exchange of gifts of precious stones, gold rings and a letter from the Kandy king expressing ‘friendship of his friends and enmity of his enemies’, Spilbergen made the long, treacherous journey to meet King Vimaladharmasuriya in Kandy. As Spilbergen made his way from Matelaco to Kandy, he observed numerous Buddhist pagodas, statues, ceremonies and religious architecture. The envoys travelled through the town of Vintane, which is marked on Zelon with a small pagoda. In Vintane they were greeted ‘by men with pipes, drums, horns and other musical instruments’, illustrated in a plan of the town. In the engraving, Spilbergen and his men approach from the river in the foreground. Musicians, monks, soldiers and elephants process through the streets towards the focal point– a large pagoda in the town’s centre. The text vividly describes a ‘very beautiful and high’ pagoda that is ‘all white with a gilded top and built like a pyramid, rising upwards oval wise up to a four-cornered point’. It moves from a description of the pagoda to the monastery, marked with an ‘8’ in the top right corner. The monastery is described as ‘similar to those of ours in this country, surrounded by galleries and many private chapels which are gilded and contain many gures of men and women whom they say have lived holy lives. These carved gures stand adorned with cloths painted silver.’",
      "dateCreated": "1613",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "kingdom-of-kandy-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "tc33",
      "smallPath": "_m/t/c/3/3/kingdom-of-kandy-wp/vintane-in-india-orientalis-ce-small.webp"
